<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Cardiopulmonary%20exercise%20testing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/TestOrMeasurement> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_n0015/tu_0001> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Spirometry (airflow limitation should be classified based on post-bronchodilator FEV1 (GOLD grade 1 to 4)) Symptoms should be assessed based on the modified MRC dyspnoea scale, and the COPD assessment tool. Together with the history of exacerbations, COPD can be grouped in stages A to D. Cardiopulmonary exercise testing (exercise capacity, differentiation of the leading cause of a reduced exercise capacity, definition of training zones based on the first ventilatory threshold) is the preferred exercise test, in addition to six minute walk test Echocardiography (exclusion/diagnosis of pulmonary hypertension; cor pulmonale)" .
